messages:
Maria Chen: FYI received an urgent customer report from a private deploy (ACME). Tool/function call is failing validation with both an additionalProperties error in a nested object and a type mismatch on price. Customer sees a 400 + validation error after a ~800ms latency spike. Repro steps and sample below.

Raj Patel: Can you paste the exact request and validator error? Also which model/route and private version are they on?

Maria Chen: Route: POST /v1/invoke/tool/charge, private deploy v1.12.4 (region-eu). Error from gateway logs: 
```
ERROR validation: toolcall validation failed: additionalProperties ["promo_code"] not allowed at /billing/items/0/metadata; expected number at /billing/items/0/price (got string)
module: rdx-validator v3.7.1
request_id: req_2f7b9c
latency_ms: 812
status: 400
```
Sample payload customer sent (redacted):
```json
{
  "customer_id": "acct_123",
  "billing": {
    "currency": "USD",
    "items": [
      {
        "sku": "plan_pro",
        "price": "12.00",     // string instead of number
        "metadata": {
          "promo_code": "SPRING2026", // unexpected key
          "region": "eu-west"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
They say this worked before last week; started after a gateway patch.

Dylan Nguyen: Likely two things: (1) the validator was tightened in the last release (PR #4821) to reject additionalProperties in nested metadata objects, and (2) we switched off coercion for numeric strings in private deploys to be strict for compliance. That explains the price string -> number rejection.

Raj Patel: Repro locally with private config: I ran the payload against local rdx-validator@3.7.1 and got the same two errors. Quick repro curl: 
```bash
curl -s -X POST https://private.example/v1/invoke/tool/charge \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer x' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d @payload.json
```
Logs align.

Maria Chen: Customer is blocked in production (billing flow). They asked for workaround or hotfix. They are on a locked compliance image so we need a safe path.

Raj Patel: Options: 
- Short term: add a gateway shim that coerces numeric strings to numbers and strips unknown metadata keys before validation (cheap patch).
- Medium: update JSON Schema for billing.items[].metadata to allow additionalProperties: true OR explicitly include promo_code as allowed field.
- Long term: improve validator error message to indicate both causes separately and provide remediation guidance to callers.

Dylan Nguyen: I can drop a small gateway shim as a canary to the customer's private cluster (no schema change). Patch idea (pseudo):
```js
// gateway-shim: coerce & strip unknown metadata
function normalizeBilling(payload) {
  payload.billing.items = payload.billing.items.map(item => {
    if (typeof item.price === 'string') item.price = parseFloat(item.price);
    if (item.metadata && typeof item.metadata === 'object') {
      // allowed metadata keys: region, source, note
      const allowed = ['region','source','note'];
      Object.keys(item.metadata).forEach(k => {
        if (!allowed.includes(k)) delete item.metadata[k];
      });
    }
    return item;
  });
  return payload;
}
```
This should restore compatibility for most callers and avoid schema changes while we align the schema.

Maria Chen: Sounds good. Can you canary that patch to the customer's private instance? Need an ETA to share with them. I'm on the call at 15:30 UTC.

Dylan Nguyen: Will schedule canary deploy in region-eu today. Rolling to single tenant node first, then monitor 30m. ETA ~ 2 hours. @ops-bot can you create a canary deploy ticket?

ops-bot: Canary deploy ticket created: CANARY-9081. Scheduled by dylan for 1745611400. Notifying oncall @eng-sre.

Raj Patel: After canary, I'll follow with a validator config tweak for private images: re-enable coerceTypes in validator config (coerceNumbers: true) behind a feature flag so customers can opt-in. Then we'll open a schema PR to explicitly permit common promo keys or document metadata contract.

Maria Chen: Great — please keep me posted. I'll offer the customer the shim workaround and ETA. Also logging this for billing escalations team and legal (since private deploy).

Dylan Nguyen: Quick note for postmortem: failing silently on additionalProperties + type mismatch created hard-to-parse error. We'll split error surface so callers get distinct errors (e.g., "invalid type for /billing/items/0/price" vs "unexpected field /billing/items/0/metadata/promo_code").

Maria Chen: Thanks team. If the canary goes green, we'll push patch and then plan a schema update next week.

ops-bot: Deploy started: CANARY-9081 -> node tenant-eu-77 at 1745611400. Will post status updates here.
